{"id": "EUVD-2026-59521", "enisaUuid": "904b26e6-aa62-39a7-b43e-f69f92da8de4", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmd/raid1,raid10: fix error-path detection with md_cloned_bio()\n\nDetect the error path using md_cloned_bio() instead of relying\non r1_bio in raid1 or r10_bio->read_slot in raid10, which may be\nNULL or -1 after splitting and resubmitting a failed bio.\n\nAs a result, the error path may not be recognized and memory\nallocations can incorrectly use GFP_NOIO instead of\n(GFP_NOIO | __GFP_HIGH), which can lead to a deadlock under\nmemory pressure.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:58:53", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:45:31", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/80eaeae0e4b1ed2418fd2b9088238651fb51df69", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8719aa0f57955fd641f952d16e02fc6b4934c6e3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/029b363c9b690613141338436ac91366b1928af2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/20fb582c92fd64e5c8bd83c6176264b2794603b7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/811545e0926d02a6a0b1a1258bb5544777c164d4"], "aliases": ["GHSA-mr8x-hvpc-q7pw", "CVE-2026-74374"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.63, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "028ae171-7904-3356-a5f1-88438ad13296", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "689389a06ce79fdced85b5115717f71c71e623e0 <811545e0926d02a6a0b1a1258bb5544777c164d4"}, {"id": "49c4f62e-bd2b-3d50-9d2c-c91094dde4f2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "4ee76c12-f22e-328c-854b-50da84b81981", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "689389a06ce79fdced85b5115717f71c71e623e0 <20fb582c92fd64e5c8bd83c6176264b2794603b7"}, {"id": "6146a0ab-9dad-3d2c-abea-0d08b3f64368", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "